// Figure artwork for the stretch routine — one filled path per pose.
//
// Split out of js/stretches.js on purpose: this is ~47 KB of path data and
// nothing here is meant to be read or hand-edited. Keeping it separate leaves
// the routine itself (names, cues, timing) short enough to open on a phone,
// which is how this repo actually gets edited.
//
// Each entry is a single <path> filled with `currentColor`, so the figures
// take the app's text colour and flip with the light/dark theme — the same
// trick the icons in ui.js use. No stroke, no fills of their own, no
// background: the white shapes the source files used to paint the body
// interior were dropped, because "white" is not a colour this app can assume.
//
// The `viewBox` on each is a square centred on that pose's real bounding box
// with a 5% margin, so every figure fills its frame by the same amount without
// any of them being stretched.
//
// **Do not "optimise" the numbers on the Illustrator-exported figures** — the
// eleven originals are full of *relative* commands, and rounding each delta
// accumulates error along the chain until the interior contours stop closing
// and the figure floods into a solid silhouette. That cost a full rebuild once
// (v26); the bounding box gave it away before the render did, a 763×560 pose
// reporting 467×51.
//
// Figures traced from a PNG (potrace, v47 onward — `ankle-rock` is the first)
// are *absolute* M/C/L/Z only, so each point stands alone and rounding cannot
// accumulate. They ship rounded to 2dp: 18 KB down to 7 KB, checked by
// rendering both at 400px and diffing — 32 antialiasing-level pixels out of
// 160,000, invisible at the 190px and 52px these are actually drawn at. Check
// which kind you have before touching a number, and re-render if you do.

